## 2. WORKSPACE CONVENTIONS & CURSOR RULES (.cursor/rules/)
Strictly adhere to:
- 00-global-development.mdc: Workspace hygiene, zero untyped code.
- 10-web-nextjs.mdc: Next.js / React best practices, SSR hydration safety, zero layout shifts.
- 11-mobile-react-native.mdc: Mobile architecture & cross-platform conventions.
- 20-security-and-data.mdc: Strict data handling and zero credential leakage.
- 30-testing-and-verification.mdc: Automated proof of completion before closing tasks.
- 40-agent-workflow.mdc: Atomic commits, state-gated execution, and ref-only GSAP listeners.

## 3. CORE ARCHITECTURE & SYSTEM MEMORY
Cross-reference and preserve the directives in:
- ARCHITECTURE.md (System design & scroll sequencing pipelines)
- MEMORY.md (Project state, progress ledger, and constraints)

## 4. CONNECTED MCP CAPABILITIES
Utilize connected MCP tools whenever applicable:
- sequential-thinking: For planning multi-phase refactors and debugging complex state logic.
- playwright: For headless browser inspection, optical contrast probes, and verifying transitions.

## 5. NON-NEGOTIABLE GATES
On EVERY change:
- pnpm --filter @pjp/docs typecheck must pass with exit code 0.
- pnpm --filter @pjp/docs build must compile with exit code 0.
- Zero console warnings or errors. Zero layout shifts.
